[thin] These are the 2.0 mm spring leaves. Their axial-end print orientation keeps the bending direction in the layer plane. The bench trials bound this section between the leaf that tore and the thicker leaf that bent at the corners.
alternatives: The 2.6 mm trial concentrated bending at its roots. Derek requested the intermediate spring thickness after the 1.3 mm and 2.6 mm trials.
