[thin] Each lead-in tapers from the retaining nose to the 0.90 mm flat stop. This continuous face spreads the spring over the fixed ledge as the cap is lowered.
alternatives: Filling the lead-in would make the hook strike the ledge squarely. Enlarging the tip beyond the spring would occupy the clearance needed to release it in the floor pocket.
